            Worldwide
          </h2>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-image
          border-radius="10px"
          padding="10px 12px"
          width="600px"
          src="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
          alt="REPLACE_ME"
          href="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/"
        />
        <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
          <p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇱🇻 Latvia - PM resigns. </strong>Latvian PM Evika Silina has announced her resignation after her coalition government lost its parliamentary majority. The crisis began when the left-wing Progressives withdrew support following Silina’s ousting of Defense Minister Andris Spruds over Latvia’s handling of stray Ukrainian drones entering from Russia. Silina accused political rivals of putting party interests above national responsibility, while the Progressives said Spruds was being used as a scapegoat for broader defense failures (<a href="https://www.dw.com/en/latvia-prime-minister-evika-silina-resigns-over-handling-of-drone-incidents-after-coalition-allys-withdrawal/a-77159518" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">drone drama</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇺🇦 Ukraine - Zelenskyy ally arrest.</strong> Ukraine’s anti-corruption court has ordered pretrial detention for Andriy Yermak, a close ally and former chief of staff to President Volodymyr Zelenskyy, over suspected currency laundering. The court set bail at 140M hryvnias, or about $3.19M, which would allow his release before a final ruling. Yermak denies the allegations and says his lawyers will appeal. Prosecutors accuse him of involvement in a 460M-hryvnia laundering scheme linked to housing development near Kyiv (<a href="https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/europe/andriy-yermak-arrest-ukraine-zelensky-b2976329.html" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">bail bombshell</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇺🇲 USA - Senate confirms Fed Chair.</strong> Kevin Warsh has been confirmed by the US Senate as chair of the Federal Reserve, replacing Jerome Powell after a largely party-line 54-45 vote. President Trump nominated Warsh as inflation reached a three-year high and concerns grew over pressure on the Fed’s independence. Warsh told lawmakers he would take measures independently, but Democrats accused him of being too close to Trump (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/news/kevin-warsh-senate-confirmation-fed-chair/" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">Powell out</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇷🇺 Russia - Aerial strike.</strong> Russia launched a massive aerial attack on Kyiv and other Ukrainian regions, killing at least five people and injuring dozens. Ukraine said Russia fired 675 drones and 56 missiles, with air defenses intercepting most of them. Kyiv suffered heavy damage, including residential buildings, a school, a vet clinic, and other civilian infrastructure. President Volodymyr Zelensky said the strike showed Moscow does not believe the war is ending and urged Ukraine’s partners not to stay silent (<a href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260514-russia-pounds-kyiv-and-cities-across-ukraine-in-massive-air-attack-drones-missiles" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">drone barrage</a>).
</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
