          >
            Foundations
          </h2>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text
  padding="10px 12px"
  font-family="TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif;"
  color="#000000"
>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 500; margin: 0;">
    What is the Velvet Revolution?
  </h2>
</mj-text>
<mj-image
  border="1px solid #00000013"
  border-radius="10px"
  padding="10px 12px"
  width="600px"
  src="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
  alt="REPLACE_ME"
  href="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/"
/>

<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>What is it? </strong>The Velvet Revolution was a peaceful, <a href="https://www.nonviolent-conflict.org/czechoslovakias-velvet-revolution-1989/" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">student-led uprising in Czechoslovakia</a> in 1989 that brought an end to more than 40 years of communist rule. It began on 17 November 1989, when riot police violently suppressed a student march in Prague commemorating a Czech student killed by the Nazis. The brutality sparked massive public outrage and quickly transformed a permitted memorial event into a nationwide anti-communist movement.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">In the days that followed, many people filled Prague’s Wenceslas Square, ringing keys to symbolize the unlocking of liberty and the end of the regime. Dissident playwright Vaclav Havel and other activists formed Civic Forum, whose mass protests and a nationwide general strike forced the communist regime to concede power just eleven days after the initial protest. By 29 December 1989, Havel was elected as the interim president of a democratic Czechoslovakia.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Legacy: </strong>The Velvet Revolution is a key event in European history. It showed that peaceful civic measures can bring down strong regimes. This movement restored democracy in Czechoslovakia, created political liberties, and inspired democratic movements across Eastern Europe. The revolution set the stage for the country’s future as an EU member.</p>
</mj-text>
